highlight.js — kerf language extras
Version: 11.11.1 (python, typescript)
Licence: BSD-3-Clause
Source:  https://www.npmjs.com/package/highlight.js — bundled from the npm package with esbuild
         (IIFE, minified). Registers onto the window.hljs exposed by
         highlight.min.js, which must load first.

Why a second file: highlight.min.js is the suite-wide bundle, shared byte-for-byte
across the Vulos product sites so it can be diffed as one thing, and it carries
neither python nor typescript. Kerf's docs fence 67 python blocks (the SDK, the
plugin and tool-authoring guides) and 7 ts/tsx blocks (.circuit.tsx), all of
which would render as flat text on that bundle alone. Layering them here keeps
the shared file untouched.

Rebuild:
  esbuild entry.js --bundle --minify --format=iife --outfile=highlight-extras.min.js
  # entry.js:
  #   import python from 'highlight.js/lib/languages/python'
  #   import typescript from 'highlight.js/lib/languages/typescript'
  #   const h = window.hljs
  #   if (h && !h.getLanguage('python'))     h.registerLanguage('python', python)
  #   if (h && !h.getLanguage('typescript')) h.registerLanguage('typescript', typescript)

Full BSD 3-Clause text: see highlight.min.js.LICENSE beside this file.
